    "question": "Coral is reading a book that is 600 pages long.  She reads half of it in the first week, and 30 percent of the remaining pages the second week. How many pages must she read the third week in order to finish the book?",
    "question_sha256": "112c913782fdaebed52762706b6125f4dd5055a2f5e66433ae9fdf2a46a278c4",
    "responses": [
      {
        "key": "gsm8k-train-722:rich",
        "raw_call_sha256": "89a9bdf7fe1a8161202b259d9c0136de366248e3f7d5a863120152a2a6e354b1",
        "student_prefix": [
          {
            "content": "Coral is reading a book that is 600 pages long.  She reads half of it in the first week, and 30 percent of the remaining pages the second week. How many pages must she read the third week in order to finish the book?",
            "role": "user"
          }
        ],
        "student_prefix_sha256": "fa54c7aa383b20899b8ef6de2d7ce1efb05d05baf0b3463a9da5d886c0fda37e",
        "target": "The book is 600 pages long. In the first week, Coral reads half of it, which is 600 / 2 = 300 pages. This leaves 600 - 300 = 300 pages. In the second week, she reads 30% of the remaining 300 pages, which is 300 * 0.30 = 90 pages. After the second week, she has 300 - 90 = 210 pages left to read. Therefore, Coral must read 210 pages in the third week to finish the book.\n\nFINAL: 210",
